-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

MkLinux DR2 is here!  We are pleased to announce the release of MkLinux 
DR2.
The CD-ROMs have been published and (limited) FTP access is available.
(We plan to set up a dedicated server for large FTP transfers; for the
present, we'll have to make do with www.mklinux.apple.com!  So, please
have patience.)

DR2 differs *significantly* from DR1. The changes are large enough, and
sufficiently extensive, for us to request that you install DR2 from
scratch, rather than simply attempting to update an existing DR1.

By making DR2 our new "baseline" for MkLinux, we can have everyone
"reading from the same page". This will ease bug tracking, improve the
efficacy of updates and patches, etc. So, while we understand that a
system reload is a hassle, we really think it is The Right Thing to
Do.

DR2 installs as a very complete system, including the X11R6.1
distribution. This takes up quite a bit of room, but it makes
installation a snap. We hope to retain this ease of installation in the
reference release, while adding a great deal of flexibility in the
complement of installed packages.

With the release of DR2, DR1 will no longer be available or supported.
We will retain the DR1 "Help and Support" information on our Web pages,
but DR1 itself will be removed from our FTP server.

As with DR1, DR2 will be available both by anonymous FTP and on CD-ROM.
We encourage you to get the disc! Unlike FTP, CD-ROM is an efficient
and reliable medium for transferring the large amounts of data (78 MB,
compressed, for the base installation; 200 MB for the extras!) included
in MkLinux DR2, and it serves as its own backup. Feel free to share the
CD with your friends.

