-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

SQLkit v.0.98 provides a means for programs written with the Linux
FlagShip compiler (a.out version 4.3) to communicate with a Just
Logic SQL database (a.out).

Although the FlagShip compiler (a Clipper compatible compiler sold in
North America by WorkGroup Solutions, Inc. that runs under Linux and
most other Unices) provides a robust, built-in database, there may be
times when it is preferable to store data in an external SQL database. 
The Just Logic SQL Database Manager is an inexpensive and reliable 
commerical product available to Linux users. SQLkit v.0.98 provides
an API of eleven functions that may be linked to a FlagShip program.
These functions allow the FlagShip program to retrieve (select),
update, append, or delete records in a Just Logic database. Records
may be locked or unlocked to protect the integrety of the database in a
multi-user environment, and changes to the database may be committed or
rolled back under the control of the FlagShip program.

SQLkit v.0.98 comes with no warranty and is available at no cost from:

ftp://ftp.wgs.com/pub/wgs/sqlkit/sqlkit.tgz

Documentation for SQLkit may be read at:

http://www.wgs.com/sqlkit/sqlkit.html

An inexpensive commercial product supporting FlagShip version 4.4 and
ELF versions of the Just Logic Database Manager is also available. For
details email griffin@ocme.ucsf.edu.

- -- 
Thomas Griffin (griffin@ocme.ucsf.edu)

