I've uploaded a new version of CMUCL to sunsite.unc.edu. 

I hope this time it won't be erased...

The system requires about 16M to run, it only swaps a little when
recompiling itself in 32M. Use *large* swap files, at least two times as
large as our memory. 

CMU CL is a fully featured lisp, with a very good compiler that increases
speed or security if you want to. The compiler checks all declared
variables and their use.It is so good it almost makes lisp a
typed language (like C where you have to declare the type of variables)!

You need the bins-naked stuff. 

For pcl you also need pcl-image. 

For clx you need bins-naked+pcl-image+clx-package. 

For hemlock you need bins-naked+pcl-image+clx-package+hemlock-package.

CLM is untested. It should work if you have a server (see documentation
for location).

I've also provided the HyperSpec from Harlequin in the package, and 
reasonable documentation...

