Version 3.3.0 of dxpc is now available from:

    ftp://ftp.x.org/contrib/utilities/dxpc-3.3.0.tar.gz
and
    ftp://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/Incoming/dxpc-3.3.0.tar.gz
    (eventually ftp://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/X11/xutils/dxpc-3.3.0.tar.gz)


dxpc is an X protocol compressor designed to improve the
speed of X11 applications run over low-bandwidth links
(such as dialup PPP connections).

dxpc-3.3.0 is the final planned release of dxpc.  It contains
a couple of minor improvements over 3.2.0:

* Improved compression of X_FillPoly requests

* dxpc now hides the MIT-SHM shared memory extension (in order to keep
  X clients from assuming that they can use shared memory because they
  are connected a dxpc proxy that appears to be a local X server)

* Minor enhancements to the FAQ


