-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

Newt (Not Erik's Windowing Toolkit) is a library for building applications 
with text based, window based interfaces. It is built on top of John E. Davis'
slang library (available from ftp://space.mit.edu/pub/davis) which provides 
good performance and little overhead. Newt has been tested on Linux/Intel,
Linux/Alpha, and Linux/SPARC machines but should be very portable.

Newt currently supports:

	1) stacked windows (only the top window is active)
	2) background text
	3) stacked help line on the bottom of the screen
	4) color and monochrome displays
	5) many widgets:
	   a) push buttons
	   b) radio buttons
	   c) check boxes
	   d) entry boxes
	   e) labels
	   f) scrollbars
	   g) listboxes
	   h) forms (similiar to X's bulletin boards and can be nested)
	   i) multi-line textbox (display only) with wrapping and scrolling
	   j) scale (for progress meters)

Newt was used to build the install program for Red Hat's Rembrandt release
(disclaimer: Rembrandt is a BETA release available on the net only) and 
some basic configuration programs includes with Rembrandt. Is is available
for public use under the LGPL from ftp.redhat.com:/pub/redhat/code/newt.

If you have any comments about Newt, please let me know.

Erik

