-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

Lc is a very small program that functions like ls, but lists files according
to their type; it is like a cross between find and ls (in a very limited sense).
The output may not be pretty, but some people might be used to it. 

Lc will be primarily of interest to people who have studied in the University of
Waterloo, Canada, or people who have used the MKS Toolkit (whose programmers
presumably wrote lc because they were once UW students).

Lc is written by MFCF (Math Faculty Computing Facility) of the University of
Waterloo. All I did is merely tweaking the official sources so that they can
compile on Linux. Copying policy is "The usual non-profit copying policy."

The Linux distribution will be on http://www.io.org/~acli/MFCF/lc/.  It will
include a man page (missing from the official distribution) when I can find
the man page, and and an LSM when I finish one.

The original sources (which are not compilable on Linux unless you tweak the
sources like I did) are at ftp://math.uwaterloo.ca/lc/distribution.

