-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

Hi all,

I am looking for beta testers for a new utility I have written called
checkd.

Essentially, checkd sends loopback mail to remote systems and collects
the responses.  If a machine doesn't reply in a specified time frame
then an alert is logged to /var/adm/messages where it can be picked up
by something like swatch or tklogger and used to notify the admin.

A locking strategy is used to make sure that if the remote fails you
don't flood them with check messages.  For bandwidth worried people,
the messages are very small and use little resource.

Mail me if interested.

Colin Rhodes
[colinr@caa.org.au]




