dxpc is an X protocol compressor designed to improve the
speed of X11 applications run over low-bandwidth links
(such as dialup PPP connections).

The new features in release 3.1.0 are:

* Added TCP_NODELAY to the socket arguments for the TCP connection between
  the Client Proxy and Server Proxy

* Minor modifications to bit stream read/write routines for faster execution

* Client-side caching of X server's response to initial X connection init
  message, for improved application startup speed

* Improved compression of X_AllocColor requests

* Improved compression of KeymapNotify and ColormapNotify events

* Minor portability fixes


