Xmcpustate

This is a modified version of the xcpustate tool that comes with
procps-0.99a. 

The changes made only affect the display code, so it will probably work
without any problems in any future versions of procps.

This version has a Motif interface added to it, so the statistics reported
for CPU, Memory, Swap and Ether are now displayed in colored bars, where
each part (idle, user, nice, kernel and system) has it's own color.

The colors as well as the size of the different display bars can be 
changed using either command line options or by specification in a 
resource file.

It does look a little bit like the system information meter tool from
Silicon Graphics. 

A binary which is dynamically linked to the Motif 2.1 shared libraries
as well as the source for xmcpustate is available at the following URL:
http://www.xs4all.nl/~ripley/RSD/linux.html

The author of procps has been notified of the changes.

Happy Statting,
Koen D'Hondt

reach out at: ripley@xs4all.nl
Surf the Web: http://www.xs4all.nl/~ripley


