QAudio - simple sound for Qt
                             version 1.0
                         by Warwick Allison

              http://student.uq.edu.au/~s002434/qt/QAudio/


The QAudio provides for simple but useful sound in the Qt GUI Toolkit,
by utilizing the Network Audio Server (NAS). 

Using the facility, a Qt-based application can play sound files very
simply: 

QAudio::play("your_sound.wav");

NAS supports .au, .voc, .wav, .aiff, and .iff file formats, and can mix
sounds in real time! It's The Only Way To Go in a multitasking
environment (otherwise, which application gets to hog the sound
device?). 

At the above URL is the source, a Linux binary, and simple example
program. 

It's free, of course.

