cd-console 1.0 is a text-mode cd-player for linux. 1.0 is the first
publicly released version of it. Here's the beginning of the README
file:

- --
1. So how does this differ from any of the other text-mode cd players
out there?

There are two fundamental differences between cd-console and any other
text-mode cd-player I've found for linux. The first of these is that
cd-console has one-key access for tracks 1-19. No more pressing that
right arrow key for ten seconds to get to your favorite track which
happens to be 18.

The second is that cd-console has random play (or shuffle, if you want
to call it that..). This hasn't been in any other text-mode cd-player
I've found either.

You can also change cd's while the program is running.

As this project started for my own personal use, I only added
features I want in my cd-player. So, there's no time display (who
wants to know that there are exactly 1:23 minutes left of this track
and 43:54 minutes left of the whole cd?)
- --

It's currently available at sunsite.unc.edu/pub/Linux/Incoming. It
should be moved to apps/sound/cds later. The filename is
cd-console-1.0.tar.gz.

