Greetings,

I would like to announce the availability of Qist 0.74, an SGML
publishing utility for X Windows. Qist features a Tcl/Tk GUI for
parsing and formatting SGML documents to LaTeX, text and HTML.

As it happens, Qist used to be called Vinea, which used to be called
IDEA. More about the name change can be found in the README extract
below.

The new features since the previous release 0.66 include alpha state
HTML formatting, automatic support for multiple DTDs and multiple
layout mappings per DTD. A number of bugs have been fixed.

Qist can be found at http://www.uta.fi/~f1sale/qist/index.html.

Yours,

Sami Lempinen (f1sale@uta.fi)

- --------------------------------
>From the README:


QIST INFORMATION

1. General Information

  The  current  version  of Qist is 0.74, which is the first
beta distribution. I feel that the workings of  Qist  itself
have  become  stable enough to justify calling it a beta. It
is the replacement files and the Qist DTD that are  in  most
need of work.

     If  you can provide me with some groovy layout mappings
for any of the bundled DTDs or a completely  different  one,
I'd  be  deeply  grateful. After all, it is the DTDs and the
layout mappings that make this tool useful. Qist  in  itself
does nothing magnificent, save making the task of validating
and formatting a slightly easier one.

2. What Is This Name Thing Anyway?

 Qist is the third and hopefully  the  last  name  for  this
software.  The  first  one, IDEA, already stood for Interna�
tional Data Encryption Algorithm.  How  was  I  supposed  to
know?  Then  I  chose  Vinea (for Vinea Is Not an Encryption
Algorithm), which also happens  to  be  a  registered  name.
Tired  of  the whole game, I chose Qist, which may stand for
Qist Is a Silly Title if you will. It  was  just  about  the
only short combination of letters which did not bring up any
hits in Alta Vista. I aplogise for any inconvenience  I  may
have caused with my unfortunate choice of titles.

     As  before, the purpose of this release is to get feed�
back. Please report any grievances or moments of joy  to  me
(f1sale@uta.fi).


