-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----


For those who enjoy upgrading your kernel all the time, this utility is
for you.  It slices, it dices, and most importantly patches!

This bash script will, provided it knows where things are, patch from the
kernel that you are currently running to the most up to date patch that
you give it.

All it has to know is where the kernel source directory is (generally
/usr/src) and where the patches are that it needs to upgrade (defaults to
/usr/src as well).  From here you run 'pk' and it will look at your
currently linux kernel tree and try and patch the patches that you have in
the proper succession.

This currently can't deal with patches similar to the "pre" 2.0 kernels.

Chris

