-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

Hi linuxers,

The cdrom sampling utility cdda2wav v0.6 is out.

New in this version:
	To further enhance the performance, sampling is done with two
	processes and double buffers. Shared memory and semaphores are
	used to do asynchronous i/o.
	So IPC kernel support is *required*.

	A raw output format is supported (no headers, just samples).

	Output can be done to a pipe, now.

	Changes from Thomas Niederreiter's cdw-tools have been incorporated.
	Thanks, Thomas.

	Changes from Zygo Blaxell have been incorporated.
	Thanks, Zygo.

	A lot of new sample rates. The audio cd sampling rate of 44100 Hz
	can now converted to any rate, which is 88200Hz divided by an
	integral divider greater than 1 and less than 102.
	Now even 8018Hz output rate is possible. This can be used to output
	to sun pcm files. The necessary header format has been added.

	The resampling stage has been completely rewritten. Now it uses a
	quadratic interpolation scheme to obtain samples which lay inbetween
	the grid.

	The signal handling has been improved. SIGINT (ie ^C) in conjunction
	with the generic scsi interface should work now.
	This version as well as the last one needs kernel versions of 1.1.68
	or above (and is tested under 2.0).

	Now you can retrieve media catalog numbers (MCN) and international
	standard recording codes (ISRC) for at least two drives types.
	(Plextor PX45-CE and Toshiba XM3401TA).

	The index scanner should work now.

	Enhanced CD format has been tested.
	CD-Plus (aka CD-Extra) CD format has been tested. Additional
	CD-Plus information are experimental.

	Lots of bug fixes.

The LSM entry follows:
