To everyone who uses IrcII, or is looking for a better IRC client,
I have the answer!

XIRC has just been released on the 31st of August.  XIRC is a
revolutionary new IRC client for X Windows, utilizing the XForms
library.  XIRC incorporates a few new things that no other IRC
client yet offers.

One of the major features is scripting via a STDIN/STDOUT method.
This means that you can write your scripts to read from the STDIN
device, and write any corresponding information to the client in
STDOUT.  (A sample script is also included in the source distribution.)

So, to make a long story short, check out http://xirc.bitgate.com/
or get it via ftp://ftp.bitgate.com/pub/xirc/current.tar.gz.

Join the mailing list, too.  Send a message to majordomo@bitgate.com
with the words "subscribe xirc" in the body of the message.

Good luck!


