LINUX USER SUPPORT TEAM (L.U.S.T.)

Purpose:
To fill in an existing gap in the Linux world and provide users with
various services/data that are not otherwise available online.  To 
provide a clearing house for these same services.

Discussion:
The L.U.S.T. (surprised nobody thought of the name earlier!) is not
intended to be involved with programming, patching, updating, or such.
It's to support the everyday, run-of-the-mill user with various support
not offered elsewhere in the Linux world with data or services such as
the Workman Database Project described below.

As with all of the other Linux projects (okay, most of 'em), this is to
be entirely volunteer-powered and driven.  You're involvement or
occasional contribution is vital.  To join the L.U.S.T., initiate a new
project, to join a mailing list, or to get involved with an ongoing
project, send email to the addresses listed at the end of this post.

At the moment, it's only myself and a couple other users involved.  We'd
like for a LOT more people to join.  Send email if you want to get
involved, to suggest a service you'd like to see,  or to even make a
comment.

SERVICES PROVIDED
