	I've set up a new mailing list for Czech and Slovak Linux
users. It is meant to be a replacement for the old discussion list
at Palacky University, Olomouc. I will probably get a list of subscribers
of the Olomouc list and resubscribe them to my Linux list.
The list will be gatewayed to the cz.comp.linux newsgroup
(available from news servers in .CZ domain) in the near future.

	The list name is

LINUX	Diskuse o operacnim systemu Linux

and it is running at Masaryk University's listserver in Brno
(listserv@linux.cz). Mailing list's address is linux@muni.cz.
At the list we accept messages in Czech, Slovak and possibly
English language. The list is dedicated for Czech- and Slovak-speaking
users, so don't subscribe to it if you cannot speak Czech or Slovak.

	To subscribe to the list, send a mail
with the "subscribe linux" text as message body to the listserver
address. You can do it for example by running this command:

	echo subscribe linux Your Name | mail listserv@muni.cz

To leave the list, send a mail with the "unsubscribe linux" message
body to listserver's address from the same machine you subscribed
to the list. You can do it by running the following command:

	echo unsubscribe linux Your Name | mail listserv@muni.cz

	If you will have any problem with this list, feel free to mail
me at <kas@muni.cz>.

	You can also visit the "Czech Linux Homepage" at
http://www.fi.muni.cz/~kas/linux/ -- you can find there
Linux-related informations in the Czech language.

- -Jan "Yenya" Kasprzak <kas@muni.cz>

