                            Announcing UUDeview
                             -----------------


 I have released new versions of UUDeview:
     UUDeview for Unix, Version 0.5.5
     UUDeview for Windows, Version 1.0
     UUDeview for DOS, Version 0.5b


 UUDeview is a smart decoder for decoding uuencoded, xxencoded, Base64
(MIME) and BinHex encoded files. It is especially powerful when it comes
to multiple multi-part files. All you do is to save all the newsgroup
articles or emails from your mail software into a file, and UUDeview
does the necessary threading and sorting by itself.
 UUDeview is distributed under the terms of the GNU GPL, which basically
means that it is absolutely free. No registration fee is required (but I
am always fond of postcards!).
 A module for encoding of files is also included. On Unix platforms, it
is able to directly mail and/or post the encoded files.

 UUDeview is available for Unix, Windows and DOS and can be downloaded
from the UUDeview Home Page on the WWW, which also features extensive
documentation.


   http://www.uni-frankfurt.de/~fp/uudeview/


 The files can also be downloaded from the Simtel (DOS/Windows) and TSX
(Unix) ftp servers and their mirrors as
   ftp://tsx-11.mit.edu/pub/linux/sources/usr.bin/uudeview-0.5.5.tar.gz
   ftp://ftp.simtel.net/pub/simtelnet/win3/security/uudw10.zip  (Windows)
   ftp://ftp.simtel.net/pub/simtelnet/msdos/decode/uudvd05b.zip (DOS)
 These are official sites, but I do not upload every release. Visit the
Web page above to check for new versions.

 For the more adventurous, source code to UUDeview is available. Documen-
tation exists describing how you can integrate decoding support into your
own applications.

 Give it a try!
   Frank Pilhofer  (Author)
   Michael Newcomb (Windows version Co-Author)


