Clobberd has been written for Internet Service Providers who want to quota
their access. For any/all/some of your users, you can quota time per day,
and/or sell them a time 'chunk' (so to speak), which they will consume
until it runs out, regulate CPU and memory usage at any given time. If a
user has exceeded any of the above quotas, Clobberd will boot them off
(warning them first of course). Another interesting feature is that
Clobberd will allow users to 'telnet' in and find out info from it like
their time usage etc. Admin can perform simple maintenance tasks by
telneting in as well. To get a full description of what is does, do a
'less clobberd.8'.


