Just a quick note to announce to Linux users that I am making the first 
public release of the *ALPHA* C source code to a *small* scale Relational 
Database Management System I have written, which compiles and runs under
Linux 1.2.13, and gcc 2.7.0.

The system, "LEAP", is used in a number of Universities and institutions
around the world. LEAP was previously only available on MS-DOS 
machines, in binary form. The source is now freely available under
the terms of the GNU General Public License.

There is a home page which contains more information on LEAP, and details
of the mailing list for users, developers, and just plain interested
folks:

http://www.brookes.ac.uk/~e0190404/leap.html

This release is an ALPHA release (0.7.0), of version 0.11, and the
source/makefile/documentation should be treated accordingly. Over
time, further releases will be made which will support other OS
versions and compilers, and be more "user/developer friendly.

Should you have any difficulty, or questions regarding LEAP, please
feel free to drop me an e-mail, or join the e-mail discussion list,
by sending a one line e-mail to "majordomo@brookes.ac.uk" containing
the line (in the body) "subscribe leap". Postings to the list should
be made to "leap@brookes.ac.uk".

Regards,

Richard Leyton.

