Dear InterNetters,

I'm pleased to announce the first release of the C++ class library `magnum':

DESCRIPTION

The portable and extendable C++ class library `magnum' has been developed in
1995 as part of a master thesis. The purpose was to implement fast
factorisation algorithms for univariate polynomials over finite fields or the
ring of integers. The classes involved are efficient and easy to handle.

The library has been tested on the following platforms:

(1)	OS		Linux (UNIX)
	Release		1.2.0, 1.3.0, 2.0.0
	Machine		i486, i586
	Compiler	C/C++ Compiler gcc 2.6.3, 2.7.0, 2.7.1
			(version 2.7.0 introduces a memory leak, see Makefile)
	Tools		Fast lexical analyzer generator flex 2.5.1,
			Parser generator bison 1.2.4,
			Make utility make 3.74,
			Pattern scanning and processing language awk 2.15,
			Stream editor sed 2.03

(2)	OS		HP-UX (UNIX)
	Release		A.09.01, A.09.05
	Machine		9000/705, 9000/735
	Compiler	C/C++ Compiler gcc 2.6.3, 2.7.1

(3)	OS		SunOS (UNIX)
	Release		5.3
	Machine		sun4c
	Compiler	C/C++ Compiler gcc 2.6.3

It was developed on the Linux system.

PORTABILITY

There is one restriction to portability: the size of the C++ fundamental type
short must be 2 bytes, and the size of type int and type long 4 bytes. With
slightly modifications the library should also work on machines where the size
of type int is only 2 bytes (in this case please contact me). You can use the
makefile target named check to figure out the sizes of these types.

DOWNLOADING

The library is available via anonymous ftp at

	URL ftp://obelix.statistik.uni-mannheim.de/public/magnum

BUILDING AND INSTALLING

To build and install the library you need

(1)	a C++ programming language compiler, as far as possible conforming to
	the latest draft working paper by the joint ANSI X3J16 and ISO WG21
	committees.

You also should have

(2)	a make utility,
(3)	an AWK programming language interpreter,
(4)	a sed compatible stream editor,
(5)	a UNIX shell and commands cd, mv, rm, echo (or equivalents)

and optionally

(7)	a lex compatible lexical analyzer generator,
(8)	a yacc compatible parser generator,
(9)	a UNIX System V compatible install utility and finally
(10)	a complete LaTeX2e typesetting system (including AMS-LaTeX) with the
	usual style files and TeX and PostScript fonts, the index generator
	makeindex and the DVI to PostScript converter dvips.

For details about building and installing the library consult the INSTALL file
and the makefile in the library's root directory.

