-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----

Version 0.10 of ZipIt, the xforms-based graphical utility for managing
an Iomega Zip drive and disks, has been upgraded to include support for
the
Iomega Jaz drive.  The name has been changed to jaZip 0.20 to reflect
this fact, as well as to correct my blunder in naming the program after
a MacIntosh file compression utility :-).

Features of jaZip that were included in the original ZipIt program:

	-Change the write protection status of a disk.
	-Query the status of a disk.
	-Autodetection of the format of the disk in the drive.
	-One-click mounting and unmounting of disks.
	-Ejection of media.

jaZip Improvements over ZipIt 0.10 include:

	-Support for both the Jaz and Zip drives.
	-Autodetection of the drive type.
	-New icons are displayed for Jaz drive users.
	-Prompting for removal of stale mount points on the fly instead 
	 of simply failing on a mount attempt over an existing mount point.

The new program is available now at http://www.scripps.edu/~jsmith/jazip

