Release 3.1.0 of dxpc is now available from:
     ftp.x.org:/contrib/utilities/dxpc-3.1.0.tar.gz
or
     sunsite.unc.edu:/pub/Linux/Incoming/dxpc-3.1.0.tar.gz
     (eventually sunsite.unc.edu:/pub/Linux/X11/xutils/dxpc-3.1.0.tar.gz


dxpc is an X protocol compressor designed to improve the
speed of X11 applications run over low-bandwidth links
(such as dialup PPP connections).

The new features in release 3.1.0 are:

* Improved compression of X_QueryColors requests and replies

* Redesign of X_PolySegment compression

* Compression of X error messages (to improve startup speed of programs
  that generate lots of error messages by trying to allocate dozens of
  colors when the colormap is already full)

* New encoding of deltas, designed to reduce the number of bits transmitted
  for small changes in coordinates between successive geometry requests

* Very primitive color image compression (only works for 8-bit pixmaps)

* Some minor code changes for improved portability


