Announcement

This is the seventh Release 0.7 of Woven Goods for LINUX. It is a
collection
of World-Wide Web (WWW) Applications and Hypertext-based Information
about
LINUX. It is ready configured for the Slackware Distribution and
currently
tested with Version 3.1 (ELF). The new LST 2.1 Distribution contains
this
collection (Release 0.1) as an integral part with some changes.

The Collection consists of five Parts, so it can be used for multiple
purposes depending on the installed Parts:

  1. User-friendly browsing of locally available LINUX Documentation
even if
     you are not connected to the Internet.
  2. Accessing world-wide available LINUX Documentation, WWW and FTP
     Servers, Linux Newsgroups and more. This is only possible if you
are
     connected to the Internet.
  3. Providing LINUX Information via your own WWW Server. Again this is
only
     possible if you are connected to the Internet.

The five Parts of Woven Goods for LINUX are:

Part 1 - World-wide Web Browser
     The World-wide Web Browser from Netscape for X11 and Lynx for ASCII
     terminals.

Part 2 - LINUX Documents
     The LINUX Documents contain the HTML Pages of Woven Goods for
LINUX,
     FAQs, HOWTOs, LDP Documents and more in different formats like
     Hypertext Markup Language (HTML), Text and Postscript.

Part 3 - World-wide Web Server
     The Apache World-wide Web Server with additional CGI Scripts for
     Statistics, viewing MAN Pages and Counters, Glimpse Search Engine
and
     the Documentation for Apache Server.

Part 4 - Hypertext Markup Language
     The HTML-Editor asWedit allows the creation of HTML-Pages.
     Some Graphic Tools allow the creation and modification of GIFs.

Part 5 - External Viewers
     The external Viewers are nessesary to present Information which can
not
     be viewed by the WWW Browsers. Only the usefull Viewers (xanim, ia,
     mpeg_play, raplyer, str, splay, swplayer, vrweb, xpdf, etc.) are
     included which are not part of the Slackware Distribution (xv,
     ghostview, showaudio).

