30 AUGUST 1996

SOLID SERVER 2.1 FOR LINUX: POWERFUL AND COMPACT RDBMS

Solid Information Technology Ltd of Helsinki, Finland today announced
worldwide availability of the Linux version of its popular relational
database management system SOLID Server. Pilot programs with top
Linux enthusiasts in Finland indicate that SOLID Server for Linux
will become a key component in Linux-based applications and www
servers all over the world. 

"We have assembled an electronic edition of SOLID Server for Linux
and we are shipping free evaluation versions and full licenses over
the web.", says Mr Artturi Tarjanne, president and co-founder of the
company.  A single-user desktop version is priced at $99 and
multi-user versions are $199 per user. SOLID Server for Linux has
been tested successfully on various Linux distributions, including
the Caldera Network Desktop. 

"Our goal is to provide Linux software developers with added value by
giving them a powerful, fully standardised database component with a
very small footprint. This will allow them to embed SOLID Server in
their applications cost-effectively and without compromising database
functionality", continues Mr Tarjanne. 

SOLID Server 

SOLID Server is a relational database management system with native
support for SQL and ODBC. It is an industrial-strength client/server
RDBMS featuring a unique Bonsai indexing technology. SOLID Server is
available on most Windows and Unix platforms and supports all major
networking protocols. The database files are binary compatible across
platforms. SOLID Server is designed in strict adherence to standards
and is extremely compact. It is easy to install and administer, and
it has an automatic backup feature and error recovery. SOLID Server
can be deployed cost-effectively in very large numbers. 

Solid Information Technology Ltd 

The mission of Solid Information Technology Ltd is to provide
industrial-strength and cost-effective database management systems
for high-volume software and industrial systems. The company is
privately held and was established in 1992. The company is located in
Helsinki, Finland and Hoofddorp, the Netherlands. Solid Information
Technology Ltd has a global distribution agreement with Compuware
Corporation (Nasdaq: CPWR) - the world's elevent largest independent
software vendor. 

