                TeamRooms 1.0 Beta 1 Now Available!
                -----------------------------------

   This note is to announce the first public beta release of TeamRooms, 
   an Internet groupware environment that lets you work together with
   colleagues in real-time or asynchronously, using Unix, Mac and Windows.


   What is TeamRooms?
   ------------------
   TeamRooms provides "shared spaces" on the Internet allowing groups
   to share information.  These electronic team rooms provide places
   to meet in real-time, or a common locale to leave information for
   other collaborators.  TeamRooms combines real-time groupware
   technologies such as shared whiteboards, chat rooms, and customizable
   groupware applets with a persistent work environment. 

   TeamRooms evolved out of our work on GroupKit, a toolkit that makes
   it easy to build real-time groupware applications.  TeamRooms adds
   support for Mac and Windows, and also supports asynchronous work.

   If you work at all with other people, check TeamRooms out.


   Okay, okay, where do I get it?
   ------------------------------
   Information on downloading is available on our Web site:

       http://www.cpsc.ucalgary.ca/projects/grouplab/teamrooms/

   Releases are available for SunOS, Solaris, SGI, Linux, AIX, 
   Windows 95/NT, Mac 68K, and Mac PowerPC.  You'll need one of the
   Unix ones for a server, but clients run everywhere.  You don't
   need any fancy hardware like video cameras or high-speed networks.


   Anything else?
   --------------
   There is information about mailing lists on the Web site, for
   TeamRooms announcements, discussion, and bug reporting.  Your
   input is important!  Information on GroupKit and other CSCW
   projects at the University of Calgary is also available.

